From 70ba95388b20f693c9f3612725f588f123c1166b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kd229y <kevin122901@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:18:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Store PTS points as 11-bit offsets from the query-cell origin

Points are stored per query cell, so the cell coordinate (5 bits per axis)
is known when a point is read: PTS keeps only q & 2047 per axis (48 -> 33
bits, lossless). The cell token carries gx/gy/gz from S2, S3 records the
cell of every issued read and adds the origin back. cse_env_mem converts
full coordinates to offsets when loading traces, so traces are unchanged.

Testbenches: tb_cse_boundary / tb_cse_array_worst / tb_env_mem use the new
format; tb_cse_worst's far-away points (outside their cells) cannot be
represented any more, so it now places points at the cell origins and
expects HIT (the legal no-hit worst case is tb_cse_array_worst).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
